Lab Report: 2D Arrays and Matrix Operations

Name: RAO ALISHA
Course:  PROGRAMMING FUNDAMENTAL LAB
Objective:
To understand 2D array storage and traversal in C.
To perform calculations like totals, averages, and maximum values.
To learn matrix operations: transpose, determinant, cofactor, adjoint, inverse, and multiplication.
To classify matrices based on their properties (square, rectangular, diagonal, symmetric, etc.).
To apply programming logic to real-life scenarios such as student marks, cinema seats, and temperature monitoring.

Classroom Marks System
Description: Store marks of 4 students in 3 subjects. Calculate total marks per student and average per subject.
Objective: Learn row-wise and column-wise operations in 2D arrays.

Cinema Seat Booking
Description: Represent 5×6 seats (0 = available, 1 = booked). Count available seats and row with maximum bookings.
Objective: Scan arrays and apply logical checks.

Temperature Monitoring
Description: Record temperature for 7 days, 3 times/day. Find weekly max and daily average.
Objective: Practice array traversal and calculations.

3×3 Matrix Analysis
Description: Perform transpose, determinant, cofactor, adjoint, and inverse.
Objective: Understand matrix operations using nested loops.

Matrix Type Checker
Description: Identify square, rectangular, zero, identity, diagonal, scalar, triangular, symmetric, skew-symmetric, singular, row, column, null matrices.
Objective: Learn classification and logical verification of matrices.

Multiply Two Matrices
Description: Multiply two matrices (max 3×3) after validating dimensions.
Objective: Practice matrix multiplication using nested loops.
